WEBVTT

00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:32.075
filled with soft bone marrow.

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:34.655
Marrow contains fat 
and other supportive tissue,

00:00:34.655 --> 00:00:38.245
but its most essential elements 
are blood stem cells.

00:00:38.245 --> 00:00:40.952
These stem cells are constantly dividing.

00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:43.305
They can differentiate 
into red blood cells,

00:00:43.305 --> 00:00:45.505
white blood cells, and platelets,

00:00:45.505 --> 00:00:48.145
and send about hundreds of billions 
of new blood cells

00:00:48.145 --> 00:00:50.775
into circulation every day.

00:00:50.775 --> 00:00:52.805
These new cells enter the bloodstream

00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:56.071
through holes 
in small capillaries in the marrow.

00:00:56.071 --> 00:00:57.351
Through the capillaries,

00:00:57.351 --> 00:01:01.021
they reach larger blood vessels 
and exit the bone.